{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Transhumanism.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Transhumanism.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"transhumanism transhumanism","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Transhumanism.md","fileName":"Transhumanism.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Transhumanism","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Futures and Human Identity]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","Posthumanism","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Transhumanism.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Transhumanism.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"transhumanism transhumanism","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Transhumanism.md","fileName":"Transhumanism.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Transhumanism","heading":"Transhumanism","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Transhumanism supports using science and technology to overcome limits of the human condition, including limits on cognition, health, lifespan, and bodily capability. AI appears in transhumanist visions as an enhancement, a partner with which humans might merge, or a route toward intelligence and life no longer constrained by the biological body.\n\nThe vision raises questions about access, inequality, and what counts as improvement. It can also express a desire to escape embodiment and earthly dependence. [[Posthumanism]] challenges human centrality from another direction: instead of perfecting humanity, it questions why human traits should define intelligence and value in the first place.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","Posthumanism","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Transhumanism.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Transhumanism.md"